    work: ["Prepared the order, cost, campaign, delivery, refund and inventory tables in Power Query so that identifiers, dates, channel names and product categories matched, then removed duplicate and incomplete records before any measure was built.", "Related the tables in a star-style model so one order, one campaign or one stock line is counted once, whatever filter is applied. This stops costs and sales from being double counted when a page is filtered by channel, category or quarter.", "Wrote the measures in DAX. Gross margin is gross profit divided by net sales. Contribution profit is net sales less cost of goods, courier cost, payment fees, return margin loss and marketing spend. Contribution margin is that profit divided by net sales, and cost to serve is the delivery and servicing cost as a share of sales.", "Built a walk from ₦100 of sales to the amount kept, so each cost is shown in order rather than as a separate figure. This is the visual that explains the 3.57.", "Compared every campaign's attributed gross profit with its cost, and compared each channel's gross profit with the fees and delivery costs it carries.", "Aged the stock against 180 days, compared stock value with demand, and listed the lines that were out of stock.", "Modelled five recovery measures on a separate page, with the assumptions shown, so the estimate can be challenged and is never read as an achieved result."],
